all right in other news now Israel has  deported a Palestinian French human  rights lawyer and activist after his  Jerusalem residency rights were revoked  earlier this month Salah hamuri had been  detained without charge since March  under so-called administrative detention  Israeli authorities have imprisoned him  several times alleging his involvement  in an assassination plot of a former  Chief Rabbi he was also branded a  terrorist by Israel as a member of the  popular front for the liberation of  Palestine Rob McBride is following  developments for us from West Jerusalem  hello there Rob what more can you tell  us about this deportation  yeah the interior ministry here uh  confirmed that tamori was put on a plane  early Thursday morning Bound for Paris  uh so bringing to an end his long fight  against deportation he is a a  Palestinian French human rights lawyer  also activist but according to the  Israelis he is a terrorist they say he's  been involved with a terrorist  organization uh that he has served  several times in prison his longest uh  prison stretch was seven years and that  was after a plea agreement in the  alleged plot to assassinate a former  Chief Rabbi and also a spiritual leader  here now after he was released from that  sentence the according to the  authorities he was still involved in  what they say were terrorist activities  they revoked his Jerusalem residency  it's this residency status that  Palestinians in the occupied East  Jerusalem live under and once that was  revoked because he is a dual National  with French citizenship it then opened  the way for him to be deported to France  but he has never spent any length of  time in France although he has a French  wife and his children who are in France  themselves  Jerusalem has always been his home so it  has raised serious concerns from human  rights groups here that the authorities  could use this to Target other activists  it's also raise concerns in France  itself and Rob just briefly what is the  what do they mean when they say that  they've put him in administrative  detention  yeah this has highlighted this very  controversial practice whereby somebody  can be detained for months at a time and  then you can get an extension to that  where they don't charge you with  anything and they don't even tell you  what you are being held under according  to the authorities this is so that they  can protect sensitive intelligence which  might lead to other attacks but  according to opponents of this it's  simply being used by the authorities to  lock up people that they don't like and  it is at the moment there are more than  800 Palestinians being held under this  controversial administrative detention  in Israeli prisons  all right we appreciate it thank you  very much Rob McBride live for us there  in West Jerusalem
 

